A||N||8||leetee@webaccess.net||Fixing a Flat on a lowered fiero||||1||
Z||000000||leetee@webaccess.net||05-27-2001||11:55 PM||||I have recently purchased a Ferrari/Fiero 355.  It is about 4.5 inches of the ground and has 17 inch wheels with low profile tires (40 and 45).  I think if I get a flat, the car will almost be bottomed, maybe only 2" clearance.  Anyone out there know how to deal with this?  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||sqoach||05-28-2001||12:06 AM||||Find someone really strong to lift up the car while you slide the jack under there  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach2.JPG">   <BR>84 SE (project car?)<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)<BR>86 SC (daily driver)||||reg||12
Z||000002||V8Fiero||05-28-2001||12:06 AM||||Keep a can of fix a flat with you at all times. Then you can drive to a garage to get the tire repaired. I used to drive a mini truck that was WAYY TOO low. This is what I did. Even had to use it once.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>86 SE Gold<BR>84 SE V8 (FS or trade)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Pffsig_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
