Z||000004||tgowens||05-28-2001||12:20 AM||||just turn it over, it's only flat on one side!!||||reg||1
Z||000005||saleenfiero||05-28-2001||12:34 AM||||I don't know if this helps, but on my old slammed Saleen stang, I used the scissor jack to jack it up enough to get a real jack under there, seemed to work.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Philphine||05-28-2001||03:35 AM||||once in lowrider mag someone was adverising a floor jack that colasped down to a few inches. don't know if it's still available or who made it. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Phil||05-28-2001||07:08 AM||||Carry 2 short pieces of 2x6 in the trunk. If and when you get a flat drive up on the 2x6's and then you can get your jack under the car.||||reg||1
